                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_46">Beeleigh, Essex.
                        Premonstratensian abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St Nicholas</orgName><p>'ecclesie sancte Marie et sancti Nicholai De Meldone' (on
                        flyleaf at end, fol. 120, s. xiii).</p><p>Beeleigh was called Maldon until
                        the thirteenth cent. 'De Meldone' in the inscription is erased and not quite
                        legible, but there can be no doubt about the reading since 'de Meldon'' is
                        scribbled twice below. The inscription is more probably a 'probatio penne'
                        than a formal ex libris.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Jacobus Riddings vicarius de Penkrich iure
                     habet hunc codicem' (s. xvi/xvii).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">The numeral 21 inside a box on fol. v is a
                     17th-cent. Bodleian number.</provenance>
               </history>
